{
  "note": [
    "Shuttle Car Alfie's fabric (DR-106), cut from the one vehicle layout in scripts/fabric-shuttle.mjs, where the car and both its control cabins are placed once in the passenger cabin's frame -- regenerate from there, do not hand-edit. SHUTTLE-CAR-ALFIE.metadata.json v2: 12 x 3.4 x 4.8, the eye at the middle.",
    "Three openings: the 2.6 x 2.5 platform doorway north, with no leaf of its own, and the 1.5 x 2.4 end doorways east and west, both of them SHUTTLE-DOOR -- open and invisible at a station, a closed sliding leaf in each while the car moves. Benches along the long walls over the west half (18 seats at 0.55 m of pitch), the freight deck clear east of them with its three tie-down rails, as LAWANDA-PLATFORM's accepted painting shows it through the open door. The view plan's seams at 135 and 225 fall midway along the benches, on a repeating run, which is the least awkward place a seam can land on a furnished wall.",
    "North, one hole and two destinations, by ALFIE-AT-KALAMONTEE: across a 6 x 4.2 berth whose centre is 0.5 m east of this door, Kalamontee Platform or Lawanda Platform -- the same 16 x 6 x 10 concrete shell, deck flush with this one, the far wall 12.7 m off with Betty's berth in it (empty unless she is standing at this station too). Neither station's own ends are in the cone: no Waiting Area portal, no escalator, no station sign. East and west, each control cabin end-on -- the panel with its slot, lever and display under the forward window, and through the window the tunnel at the live end or a concrete buffer close to at the dead one. While SHUTTLE-MOVING the north doorway is shut, both end leaves are closed and the bore runs on past the door."
  ],
